# SEO Migration Requirements

Google does not penalize a platform change if URLs, content, and metadata stay equivalent. Migration losses come from technical mistakes.

## Must preserve (when migrating or building pages)

- Identical URLs (including trailing slash policy)
- Title tags, meta descriptions, canonical tags, Open Graph tags
- Heading hierarchy (H1, H2, H3) and internal links
- Image alt text, structured data (schema), breadcrumbs
- Correct robots.txt and XML sitemap
- HTTP 200 or proper 301 redirects for any URL changes

## Avoid

- Changing URLs without 301 redirects
- `Disallow: /` or leftover `noindex` from staging
- Altering metadata, headings, or internal linking without reason
- Blocking crawlers or omitting sitemap submission after launch

## Can improve SEO when done well

- Faster load times, cleaner HTML, better Core Web Vitals
- Less unnecessary JavaScript, optimized images, better TTFB
